1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,770
50 % profit in 45 days.

2
00:00:03,650 --> 00:00:04,670
Boston, 1920.

3
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:06,810
Banks paid 5 % a year.

4
00:00:07,090 --> 00:00:09,600
Charles Ponzi said he bought postal coupons cheap

5
00:00:09,610 --> 00:00:12,050
in Europe and cashed them in America.

6
00:00:12,710 --> 00:00:13,590
Thousands lined up.

7
00:00:13,670 --> 00:00:16,350
Even most of Boston's police force bought in.

8
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:17,530
But do the math.

9
00:00:17,730 --> 00:00:21,390
To pay everyone, he'd need 160 million coupons.

10
00:00:21,890 --> 00:00:23,970
There were about 27 ,000.

11
00:00:24,310 --> 00:00:26,750
So the profits came from the next investor.

12
00:00:27,010 --> 00:00:28,660
Then a newspaper checked the numbers.

13
00:00:28,670 --> 00:00:30,710
The line turned into a run.

14
00:00:30,950 --> 00:00:32,210
Six banks went down.

15
00:00:32,410 --> 00:00:33,230
$20 million.

16
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:34,250
Gone.

17
00:00:34,770 --> 00:00:36,690
His name became the word for it.

18
00:00:36,850 --> 00:00:37,830
He died broke.

19
00:00:38,390 --> 00:00:40,050
Total estate, $75.
